The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
throw new IOException(e);
```
Reason:
The IPC client was catching `ExecutionException` and uniformly throwing an `IOException` regardless of the actual underlying exception. This behavior obscured the original exception type, making it impossible for callers to handle specific exceptions correctly.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
Throwable cause = e.getCause();
if (cause instanceof IOException) {
  throw (IOException) cause;
} else {
  throw new IOException(cause);
}
```
Reason:
The patch retrieves the original cause of the `ExecutionException` and checks if it is an instance of `IOException`. If it is, it rethrows it as such; otherwise, it wraps it in an `IOException`. This approach preserves the original exception type when appropriate, allowing callers to handle exceptions more accurately based on their specific types.

